In the context of secure coding practices, what is a potential consequence of including the same header file multiple times in a C/C++ program, as seen in the code below?

#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>

Choose the most appropriate consequence.

You are reviewing the security of a web application designed to run database backups using a privileged user account. The application uses the following command to initiate the backup and cleanup process:

java
String btype = request.getParameter("backuptype");
String cmd = new String("cmd.exe /K \"c:\util\rmanDB.bat "+btype+"&&c:\utl\cleanup.bat\"")
System.Runtime.getRuntime().exec(cmd);


What is a potential security risk associated with the above implementation, and how could it be mitigated?
